# sem-property — UX design brief for the image model
#
# Design the reference experience for <sem-property>, the key/value
# assertion row of a SemText definition block. One example page per
# display mode, using the attached captures of the CURRENT production
# render as the baseline to refine, not to replace. Dark theme (the site
# chrome is dark-only), type-led, no decorative art: this is a reading
# surface for machine-checkable definitions.
schema: "0.4"
id: sem-property-ux-modes
type: image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    Design sheet for the SemText "sem-property" element: one key/value
    assertion inside a definition block. Render six example pages, one per
    display mode, each as a plausible docs-site viewport screenshot in the
    attached dark theme (near-black page, elevated card surface, single
    accent, muted key column).

    Mode 1 — default row (reference: primary render): a bordered rounded
    container of stacked rows; each row is a two-column grid. Key column
    (left, min 8rem): the term in small-caps, muted colour — attr(key) is
    display-only. Value column (right, wider): the property text, normal
    body type, fully legible. Alternate rows carry a barely-lighter surface
    tint. The pair reads as term :: value at a glance.

    Mode 2 — multi-line value: same grid, but a value authored on two
    lines renders on two lines (authored whitespace is preserved, never
    collapsed, never ellipsized). Keys still wrap as free text.

    Mode 3 — glossary term (view-as="glossary"): the block restacks —
    term as a bold upright heading line, its definition directly under it,
    one term card per property. Each term card is an anchor target: show a
    prose sentence above the block with two accent-coloured links to terms,
    and one link in its hover state with a small preview popover floating
    under the anchor showing the bold term and its value. Popover has a
    subtle border, shadow, role=tooltip affordance; Esc-closable.

    Mode 4 — compact "::" sugar with key: a row whose value text is
    "ttl :: 15m" renders verbatim in the value column while the key column
    still shows the canonical term from the key attribute (key wins).

    Mode 5 — sugar without key (honest failure mode): one row with NO key
    authored — the raw text "storage :: httpOnly cookie" sits in the value
    column, no term is drawn, nothing is hidden. Show it as a clearly
    readable, unstyled row that still invites the author to add key.

    Mode 6 — narrow viewport (390px): the grid collapses to key stacked
    above value; rows keep their tint; long unbroken tokens in values wrap
    instead of overflowing.

    Every page: language en, left-aligned, generous line-height, AA
    contrast, focus-visible ring on the glossary links, no scrollbars, no
    decorative imagery — the design must read as quiet, technical,
    documentation-grade.
  negative: >-
    occluded or blurred value text, spoiler-style hiding, gradient art,
    illustrations, mascots, watermarks, more than one accent colour,
    truncated values with ellipses, monospace value text in default mode,
    bright white cards, drop caps, justified text
  style: >-
    minimal-tech dark documentation UI; small-caps muted labels; 1px hairline
    borders; 12px radius; single violet accent used sparingly for links and
    focus states
attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-property-dist/sem-property-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    note: baseline default-row render, 1280px
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-property-dist/sem-property-multiline-value-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    note: baseline multi-line value render (whitespace preserved)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-property-dist/sem-property-glossary-term-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    note: baseline glossary view with prose anchors
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-property-dist/sem-property-sugar-keyless-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    note: baseline "::" sugar rows, key wins / keyless verbatim
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-property-dist/sem-property-class-form-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    note: baseline class-form alias (renders identically to element form)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-property-dist/sem-property-primary-render-390.png
    role: reference
    note: baseline narrow-viewport collapse (key above value)
output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-property-ux-modes.png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
requirements:
  text_fidelity: labels and values in the reference captures must stay
    readable where reused; do not paraphrase keys or values
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    mode_coverage:
      weight: 0.3
      description: all six modes present as distinct example pages
      fail_signals:
        - fewer than six distinct pages
        - modes merged into one collage page
    term_value_reading:
      weight: 0.3
      description: every default-mode row reads unambiguously as term :: value
      fail_signals:
        - key rendered in body weight or accent colour
        - value occluded, blurred, truncated, or styled as code
    glossary_affordances:
      weight: 0.2
      description: glossary mode shows stacked term/definition and one hover preview popover
      fail_signals:
        - popover hiding or replacing prose
        - no visible anchor affordance on prose links
    whitespace_honesty:
      weight: 0.1
      description: multi-line values keep their line breaks
      fail_signals:
        - values reflowed to one line
    theme_discipline:
      weight: 0.1
      description: dark documentation-grade surface, single accent, no decorative art
      fail_signals:
        - multiple accent hues
        - illustration or watermark present
  reject_if:
    - any value text is unreadable or occluded
    - any key column missing while a key is authored
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-property
  - reference-ux
